  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "It's known that there is a strong negative linear correlation between the variables $x$ and $y.$ Which of the following scatter plots corresponds to this situation?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine the given situation.\n\n- The *negative* linear correlation means that the data points should be scattered along a line with a *negative* slope.\n\n- Since the correlation is *strong*, most of the points should be scattered *close* to the trend line.\n\nTherefore, this situation corresponds to the following scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14226558/assets/8ca401fd830f94dae1f40d024af0362491165f91cbde4cb6fb783124e241ca4b.png)",
